window.LC_CHUNKS=window.LC_CHUNKS||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["university_electrical_engineering_en"]=window.LC_CHUNKS["university_electrical_engineering_en"]||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["university_electrical_engineering_en"][24]={"university_electrical_engineering_en:M24-L1":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L1\">M24-L1 – Microcontrollers and C: Registers, Bit Masks and Peripheral Interfaces<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M24 – Bachelor–Master Bridge: Transition to Embedded Systems<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor · Bachelor–Master Bridge<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M15&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M15-L1<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M23&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M23-L3<\/a>, basic\nC programming.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Formulate register operations\ncorrectly and recognise their limitations with real peripherals.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Diagnostic self-test<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">What distinguishes a microcontroller from a standalone logic device?\n2. What is the difference between a register as a hardware state and a C\nvariable in RAM? 3. Why cannot an individual status bit always be\ncleared by an ordinary write?<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><strong>Answers:<\/strong> 1. CPU, memory and peripherals are\nintegrated. 2. A peripheral access can trigger hardware actions in\naddition to accessing the stored value. 3. The semantics depend on the\ndata sheet; for example, with write-one-to-clear, writing a one clears\nan event bit.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Address space and peripherals<\/h2>\n<p>A microcontroller combines a processor core, memory, clock sources\nand interfaces. The CPU addresses memory and peripheral registers via a\nbus. Memory-mapped I/O (MMIO) allows device registers to be accessed\nthrough designated addresses. Address decoding selects hardware: a read\ncan remove a FIFO entry; a write can start a timer. A register is\ntherefore not necessarily an ordinary memory cell.<\/p>\n<p>Typical functional blocks:<\/p>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<\/colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Block<\/th>\n<th>Function<\/th>\n<th>Verifiable property<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>GPIO<\/td>\n<td>Digital input/output<\/td>\n<td>Levels, direction, pin assignment<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ADC<\/td>\n<td>Analogue-to-digital conversion<\/td>\n<td>Reference, resolution, conversion time<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Timer<\/td>\n<td>Time base, trigger<\/td>\n<td>Prescaler, counting range, period<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SPI / I²C<\/td>\n<td>Communication<\/td>\n<td>Clock, protocol, electrical constraints<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DMA<\/td>\n<td>Transfer without CPU copying each word<\/td>\n<td>Memory boundaries, coherency, completion event<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>The abstract registers in this lesson have <strong>no real\naddresses<\/strong>. Register fields, reset values and side effects must\nbe obtained from the reference manual of the target device. CMSIS\nillustrates how a specific processor core can be accessed through\nstructured register definitions.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-and-information-technology-en/media/img/U_EIT_097_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Abstract microcontroller data path and three bit operations on an example 8-bit register.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: The abstracted microcontroller connects memory and\nperipheral registers; setting, clearing and masking individual bits\nselectively change an example register.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Derivation of bit operations<\/h2>\n<p>An unsigned word\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>r<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>w<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nbits can be written as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><msubsup><mo>∑<\/mo><mrow><mi>i<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><mrow><mi>w<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msubsup><msub><mi>b<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mi>i<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=\\sum_{i=0}^{w-1}b_i2^i<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe mask for bit\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mi>k<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=2^k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nOR sets a selected bit; AND with the inverted mask clears it; XOR\ntoggles it. AND with the original mask isolates the bit. For a field of\nwidth\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nstarting at bit\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nprovided\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>w<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n&lt;w<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>w<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k+n\\le w<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe mask is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mi>k<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=(2^n-1)2^k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nthe replacement is<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>r<\/mi><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mi>&amp;<\/mi><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mo>∼<\/mo><mi>m<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>v<\/mi><mo>≪<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mi>&amp;<\/mi><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mi>m<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r_{\\mathrm{neu}}=(r\\ \\&amp;\\ \\sim m)\\ |\\ ((v\\ll k)\\ \\&amp;\\ m).<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>The original subscript neu denotes the new value. This notation\ndenotes bitwise AND, complement, OR and left shift. First check the\nfield value\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nagainst\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>v<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le v&lt;2^n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nif an oversized value is to be treated as an error.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Example:<\/strong> An ordinary 8-bit R/W register contains\n<code>0x52<\/code> (<code>01010010<\/code>). Setting bit 0 gives\n<code>0x53<\/code>; clearing bit 4 of the original value gives\n<code>0x42<\/code>; toggling bit 6 gives <code>0x12<\/code>. Setting field\n[3:2] to 3 gives <code>0x5E<\/code>. Each operation is calculated\nindependently from the original value.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>C and safe access<\/h2>\n<p>The following host example models only an R/W register; no hardware\nis addressed.<\/p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre class=\"sourceCode c\"><code class=\"sourceCode c\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><a href=\"#cb1-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"pp\">#include <\/span><span class=\"im\">&lt;stdint.h&gt;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"><a href=\"#cb1-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"pp\">#include <\/span><span class=\"im\">&lt;assert.h&gt;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-3\"><a href=\"#cb1-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"dt\">int<\/span> main<span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dt\">void<\/span><span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-4\"><a href=\"#cb1-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"dt\">uint8_t<\/span> r <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"bn\">0x52<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"><a href=\"#cb1-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    assert<span class=\"op\">((<\/span><span class=\"dt\">uint8_t<\/span><span class=\"op\">)(<\/span>r <span class=\"op\">|<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"bn\">0x53<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">);<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-6\"><a href=\"#cb1-6\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    assert<span class=\"op\">((<\/span><span class=\"dt\">uint8_t<\/span><span class=\"op\">)(<\/span>r <span class=\"op\">&amp;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">~(<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span> <span class=\"op\">&lt;&lt;<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">4<\/span><span class=\"op\">))<\/span> <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"bn\">0x42<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">);<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-7\"><a href=\"#cb1-7\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    assert<span class=\"op\">((<\/span><span class=\"dt\">uint8_t<\/span><span class=\"op\">)(<\/span>r <span class=\"op\">^<\/span> <span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span> <span class=\"op\">&lt;&lt;<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">6<\/span><span class=\"op\">))<\/span> <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"bn\">0x12<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">);<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-8\"><a href=\"#cb1-8\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"dt\">const<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">unsigned<\/span> mask <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">3<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span> <span class=\"op\">&lt;&lt;<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-9\"><a href=\"#cb1-9\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    assert<span class=\"op\">((<\/span><span class=\"dt\">uint8_t<\/span><span class=\"op\">)((<\/span>r <span class=\"op\">&amp;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">~<\/span>mask<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">|<\/span> <span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dv\">3<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span> <span class=\"op\">&lt;&lt;<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"op\">))<\/span> <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"bn\">0x5E<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">);<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-10\"><a href=\"#cb1-10\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span><\/code><\/pre><\/div>\n<p>In firmware, MMIO accesses are usually implemented through\n<code>volatile<\/code>-qualified objects or device-specific access\nfunctions. <code>volatile<\/code> alone guarantees neither atomicity,\nthread safety, memory ordering nor correct device behaviour. A\nread-modify-write sequence reads, modifies and writes. If an interrupt\nchanges another bit in the meantime, that change may be lost. With a W1C\nstatus register, care must be taken not to write back all the bits that\nwere set when read: under the assumed W1C semantics, acknowledgement is\nperformed by writing the selected ones directly. Depending on the\nhardware, separate SET/CLR registers or protected accesses must be\nused.<\/p>\n<p>It is not valid to assume that all bit patterns, addresses and access\nwidths are portable. Even a correct C operation requires the correct\nhardware configuration.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises and review<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Clear bit 7 of <code>0xA6<\/code> and set bit 0.\n<strong>Solution:<\/strong> <code>0x27<\/code>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Extract field [5:3] from <code>0xA6<\/code>.\n<strong>Solution:<\/strong> <code>(0xA6u &gt;&gt; 3) &amp; 7u<\/code>\ngives 4.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">An 8-bit W1C register shows <code>0x09<\/code>; acknowledge bit 0\nonly. <strong>Solution:<\/strong> Write <code>0x01<\/code>; an RMW with\n<code>| 1u<\/code> could also clear bit 3.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why is a host-program test insufficient? <strong>Solution:<\/strong>\nIt tests C bit logic, not bus width, electrical properties, concurrency\nor register semantics. In the project <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M24&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M24-L5<\/a>, this\ndistinction is maintained by using a simulated sensor source.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.vvz.ethz.ch/Vorlesungsverzeichnis/lerneinheit.view?ansicht=KATALOGDATEN&amp;lang=en&amp;lerneinheitId=204662&amp;semkez=2026W\">ETH\nZürich – Embedded Systems, 227-0124-00L (Curriculum G5)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://arm-software.github.io/CMSIS_6/latest/Core/regMap_pg.html\">Arm\nCMSIS-Core – Register Mapping<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://avrdudes.github.io/avr-libc/avr-libc-user-manual/group__util__atomic.html\">AVR-LibC\n– Atomic Blocks<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_en:M24-L2":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L2\">M24-L2 – State Machines and Time-Triggered Processing<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M24 – Bachelor–Master Bridge: Transition to Embedded Systems<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor · Bachelor–Master Bridge<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M23&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M23-L3<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M12&amp;lesson=L4&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M12-L4<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Specify a non-blocking sequence\nand distinguish periodic scheduled times from actual execution\ntimes.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>States instead of blocking waits<\/h2>\n<p>A measurement node is to acquire data regularly while processing\nstatus messages and faults. A long wait loop blocks other tasks if they\nrun on the same execution path. A state machine separates waiting states\nfrom short processing actions. A typical sequence is IDLE → CONVERT →\nREADY → IDLE. On timeout, ERROR follows; error handling can return to\nIDLE in a controlled manner. Unlike a loop waiting for the ADC, the main\nloop can handle other tasks between events.<\/p>\n<p>A model consists of state\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\ninput/event\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>u<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand time\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe transition function\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mi>F<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>u<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^+=F(x,u,t)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand action\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>u<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A(x,u,t)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmust be defined separately. In a Moore model, outputs depend only on the\nstate; in a Mealy model, they also depend on current inputs. Actions on\ntransitions must be specified explicitly.<\/p>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<\/colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>State<\/th>\n<th>Condition<\/th>\n<th>Next state/action<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>IDLE<\/td>\n<td>Scheduled time reached<\/td>\n<td>CONVERT, store trigger and scheduled time<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CONVERT<\/td>\n<td>Conversion complete before/at deadline<\/td>\n<td>READY, save result<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CONVERT<\/td>\n<td>Deadline reached, no result<\/td>\n<td>ERROR, count fault<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>READY<\/td>\n<td>Record handled<\/td>\n<td>IDLE, next period<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ERROR<\/td>\n<td>Reset/recovery permitted<\/td>\n<td>IDLE, new time base according to rule<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>A priority must be defined for simultaneous events (here, valid\ncompletion at the deadline counts as on time). If the period elapses\nwhile CONVERT remains active, no second conversion is started here; the\nmissed trigger is counted. Even if a timeout leads to recovery, the\nmeasurement gap must be documented.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Periods and drift<\/h2>\n<p>A periodic task with period\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand start time\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>t<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nhas scheduled releases<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>t<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mi>T<\/mi><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r_k=t_0+kT.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>With a relative delay\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\n<em>after<\/em> processing of duration\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe result is instead\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>t<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mi>T<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_{k+1}=t_k+C_k+T<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWith constant\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe phase deviation after\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nintervals is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mi>C<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">kC<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAbsolute scheduling avoids this systematic accumulation but does not\nguarantee an immediate start. Actual release to the scheduler may be\nshifted by time quantisation and priorities.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Worked example:<\/strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T=10<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms. With relative delay, five executions start at 0, 13, 26, 39 and 52\nms. With ideal fixed periodic scheduling, the values are 0, 10, 20, 30\nand 40 ms. The fifth relative start is 12 ms late. Over a long running\ntime this corresponds to a rate of about 76.9 Hz versus 100 Hz.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-and-information-technology-en/media/img/U_EIT_098_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Sensor state transitions and comparison of fixed periods with relative delay.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: The sensor state machine distinguishes conversion,\nready and error states; fixed absolute release times avoid the\ncumulative drift of relative waiting intervals.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Tick wraparound and missed periods<\/h2>\n<p>A 32-bit tick counter with a millisecond clock wraps after\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mn>32<\/mn><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2^{32}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms, or about 49.71 days. A relational comparison\n<code>now &gt;= due<\/code> is unreliable across the boundary. The\ndifference between two <code>uint32_t<\/code> timestamps, by contrast,\ncan be interpreted modulo\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mn>2<\/mn><mn>32<\/mn><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2^{32}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor a fully observed interval shorter than one complete counter cycle,\nthe correct elapsed duration is obtained.<\/p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre class=\"sourceCode c\"><code class=\"sourceCode c\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><a href=\"#cb1-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"pp\">#include <\/span><span class=\"im\">&lt;stdint.h&gt;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"><a href=\"#cb1-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"pp\">#include <\/span><span class=\"im\">&lt;stdbool.h&gt;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-3\"><a href=\"#cb1-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"dt\">static<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">bool<\/span> elapsed<span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dt\">uint32_t<\/span> now<span class=\"op\">,<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">uint32_t<\/span> start<span class=\"op\">,<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">uint32_t<\/span> dt<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-4\"><a href=\"#cb1-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dt\">uint32_t<\/span><span class=\"op\">)(<\/span>now <span class=\"op\">-<\/span> start<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">&gt;=<\/span> dt<span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"><a href=\"#cb1-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span><\/code><\/pre><\/div>\n<p>Example: Start <code>0xFFFFFFFD<\/code>, followed by\n<code>now=2<\/code>. The difference is 5 ticks. Ordering arbitrary\ntimestamps requires an additional half-range convention; the example\nabove checks only elapsed duration from a known start.<\/p>\n<p>If invocation is late, distinguish the strategies: catch up on all\nmissed releases, skip to the next future release, or deliberately\nrestart the time base. A sensor usually cannot reconstruct past physical\nmeasurement instants. An ADC value read later must not be given the\ntimestamp of a missed measurement. In <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M24&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M24-L5<\/a>, there\nis an independent ideal producer; the consumer may be delayed\ntemporarily.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Designing a main loop<\/h2>\n<p>A cooperative main loop invokes short services: poll events, update\nthe state, acquire data and handle communication. Each service must\nbound its maximum execution time. An RTOS can put blocked tasks to sleep\nand execute other tasks; for periodic execution, an absolute release\nfunction (for example, the FreeRTOS delay-until family) can stabilise\nphase. However, an RTOS does not replace analysis of execution time,\npriorities and shared resources.<\/p>\n<p>Verification: first test transitions at the thresholds, then events\nin a different order, timeout, duplicate completion events and restart.\nAn invalid event in the wrong state should be ignored or counted rather\nthan triggering an uncontrolled transition. Timestamps for the trigger\nand data acquisition make it possible to distinguish measurement latency\nfrom processing latency afterwards.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises and review<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>20<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T=20<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms. Relative delay: how large is the start deviation after ten\nintervals? <strong>Solution:<\/strong> 40 ms.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The ADC reports completion exactly at the deadline.\n<strong>Solution:<\/strong> READY according to the priority chosen above;\nresult valid. The opposite convention could also be specified but would\nhave to be tested consistently.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A polling service sees <code>start=0xFFFFFFFE<\/code>,\n<code>now=3<\/code>. <strong>Solution:<\/strong> 5 ticks elapsed.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">With\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T=10<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms, each execution takes 12 ms. <strong>Solution:<\/strong> The desired\nfrequency cannot be sustained by a single serial consumer; an absolute\ntime base cannot create missing computing capacity.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.vvz.ethz.ch/Vorlesungsverzeichnis/lerneinheit.view?ansicht=KATALOGDATEN&amp;lang=en&amp;lerneinheitId=204662&amp;semkez=2026W\">ETH\nZürich – Embedded Systems, 227-0124-00L (Curriculum G5)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://freertos.org/Documentation/02-Kernel/04-API-references/02-Task-control/02-vTaskDelayUntil\">FreeRTOS\n– vTaskDelayUntil<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_en:M24-L3":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L3\">M24-L3 – Sampling, Timers, Interrupts and Data Buffers<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M24 – Bachelor–Master Bridge: Transition to Embedded Systems<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor · Bachelor–Master Bridge<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M16&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M16-L2<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M24&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M24-L1<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M24&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M24-L2<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Size a sampling time base and a\nbounded data buffer, and make data losses detectable.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>From the measured quantity to the timestamp<\/h2>\n<p>A sensor value without a time reference is incomplete for\ndiscrete-time signal processing. A periodic hardware timer can trigger\nthe ADC; on completion, an interrupt reports the available sample. The\ntimestamp can denote either the trigger or the actual sampling instant.\nThe time of the interrupt is not automatically identical to either. With\na hardware trigger and fixed conversion time, the timing of sampling can\nbe determined much more precisely than with a software-triggered\nindividual measurement.<\/p>\n<p>A timer with input clock\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_{\\mathrm{clk}}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\ninteger divider\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand a counter from 0 to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ninclusive produces the period in this model<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>A<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mfrac><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_s=\\frac{P(A+1)}{f_{\\mathrm{clk}}}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>At 48 MHz,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>48<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P=48<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>9999<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=9999<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe counter clock is 1 MHz and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_s=10<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms, or 100 Hz. Some devices encode the divider as the register value\nminus one, others differently. Timer mode and clock tree must also be\nchecked. For a sinusoidal signal at 40 Hz, the frequency is below the\nideal Nyquist limit of 50 Hz; higher spectral components must be limited\nby suitable analogue filters.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Interrupts and data handover<\/h2>\n<p>An interrupt service routine (ISR) responds to an event. Hardware\npriorities, masking times and higher-priority sources affect the time\nuntil processing begins. The ISR should service the device according to\nits acknowledgement rules, acquire the record with sequence number and\ntimestamp, and delegate longer processing to another context. A single\nflag for several rapid events may combine multiple samples and thus\nconceal data loss.<\/p>\n<p>A FIFO (first in, first out) preserves chronological order. For a\ncapacity\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand separate write and read indices\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>l<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h,l<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nan additional occupancy counter\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ncan be maintained. The following holds:<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>K<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><msup><mi>h<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>h<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">mod<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mi>K<\/mi><\/mrow><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><msup><mi>l<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>l<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">mod<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mi>K<\/mi><\/mrow><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le n\\le K,\\qquad h^+=(h+1)\\bmod K,\\qquad l^+=(l+1)\\bmod K.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>When the queue is full, the <strong>new<\/strong> sample is discarded\nhere (drop newest) so that previously acquired data remain in order. The\nsource sequence number is incremented even when data are lost. An\nalternative would be to overwrite the oldest sample if recency matters\nmore than the complete history. Both approaches require fault\nstatistics. A record with two 32-bit values and one 16-bit value\nrequires at least 10 bytes of payload; four records require 40 bytes,\nbut the actual size of a C array can be larger due to alignment and\npadding. The <code>sizeof<\/code> result on the target device is\nauthoritative.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-and-information-technology-en/media/img/U_EIT_099_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Sampling and processing sequence with a service gap and the evolution of FIFO occupancy.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: The service gap temporarily prevents processing from\nstarting; arriving samples fill the FIFO until buffer capacity or\ndiscards determine the subsequent course.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Calculating the buffer limit<\/h2>\n<p>A service gap of length\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nduring which no records are removed produces at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⌈<\/mo><mi>B<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⌉<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lceil B/T_s\\rceil<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nreleases at period\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin the half-open interval\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>B<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[t,t+B)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAt initial occupancy\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>n<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n_0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthis interval requires at least<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><msub><mi>n<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⌈<\/mo><mi>B<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⌉<\/mo><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K\\ge n_0+\\lceil B/T_s\\rceil.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>This does not yet account for an additional arrival before the first\nremoval at the interval boundary. Event ordering and further blocking\nmust be considered in practical sizing. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>59<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B=59<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_s=10<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n_0=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nup to six slots are required. A capacity of four causes the samples at\n70 and 80 ms to be lost in the scenario [30,89) from L5. The sample at\n30 ms is the first in the service gap.<\/p>\n<p>Long-term stability is a separate question: an average service rate\nbelow the arrival rate eventually causes loss with a finite buffer. With\na serial service time\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>12<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=12<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms, the maximum service rate is 83.3/s, while 100/s arrive. More memory\npostpones the problem but does not eliminate it. With\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms and the consumer available after the service gap, however, the\nbacklog can be cleared.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Concurrency and boundary cases<\/h2>\n<p>The FIFO in this lesson and the final lesson runs in a single\nsimulation context. A real ISR and a task share memory. They must not\nboth modify a shared occupancy counter without synchronisation. Even\nindividual multibyte accesses can be interrupted on small CPUs. Safe\nalternatives include short, correctly protected critical sections, a\nsingle-producer/single-consumer structure verified for the target system\nwith suitable memory ordering, or the designated RTOS queues. In the\nFreeRTOS example, the ISR must use the ISR-specific queue function,\ncheck the return value and account for any required context switch;\npermitted interrupt priorities depend on the port.<\/p>\n<p>The queue stores records by value; when using pointers, the lifetime\nof the referenced memory must also be ensured. Tests should cover at\nleast reading when empty, writing when full, index wraparound, reuse\nafter removal and simultaneous events at a boundary. Sequence gaps\nidentify lost samples; timestamp differences enable jitter analysis.\nHardware overrun flags are also needed because a missed trigger before\nsequence-number assignment may otherwise remain invisible.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises and review<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Timer 24 MHz, divider 24, final count 4999.\n<strong>Solution:<\/strong> 5 ms, or 200 Hz.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">An empty buffer has\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\narrivals every 10 ms, removal stops during [30,89).\n<strong>Solution:<\/strong> six arrivals, two losses with drop\nnewest.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The FIFO contains two records and the next service gap lasts 21 ms.\n<strong>Solution:<\/strong> in the worst case, three additional releases;\nat least five slots for the interval, possibly one additional slot if\nevents coincide at the boundary.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why must <code>volatile unsigned count<\/code> not be regarded as\ncomplete protection? <strong>Solution:<\/strong> an increment/decrement\noperation is a compound access; interleaving can produce an inconsistent\ncounter.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.vvz.ethz.ch/Vorlesungsverzeichnis/lerneinheit.view?ansicht=KATALOGDATEN&amp;lang=en&amp;lerneinheitId=204662&amp;semkez=2026W\">ETH\nZürich – Embedded Systems, 227-0124-00L (Curriculum G5)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://arm-software.github.io/CMSIS_6/latest/Core/group__NVIC__gr.html\">Arm\nCMSIS-Core – Interrupts and Exceptions (NVIC)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://community.freertos.org/Documentation/02-Kernel/04-API-references/06-Queues/06-xQueueSendToBackFromISR\">FreeRTOS\n– xQueueSendToBackFromISR<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://avrdudes.github.io/avr-libc/avr-libc-user-manual/group__util__atomic.html\">AVR-LibC\n– Atomic Blocks<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_en:M24-L4":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L4\">M24-L4 – Real-Time Fundamentals: Latency, Jitter and Deadlines<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M24 – Bachelor–Master Bridge: Transition to Embedded Systems<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor · Bachelor–Master Bridge<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M15&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M15-L3<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M24&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M24-L2<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M24&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M24-L3<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Evaluate deadline misses using\ndefined timing quantities and derive simple response-time bounds.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Measurable timing quantities<\/h2>\n<p>A real-time task is characterised not only by its numerical output\nbut also by the permissible time at which that output is produced. Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nbe the release time,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>s<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthe start time and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthe completion time. The start latency is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>s<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_k=s_k-r_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nand the response time is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_k=f_k-r_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\na relative deadline\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>D<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis met if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>≤<\/mo><msub><mi>D<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_k\\le D_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWhen service is uninterrupted, the processing duration\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis equal to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>s<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_k-s_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIf execution is interrupted, this difference includes the duration of\nthe interruptions and must not be equated with CPU execution time.<\/p>\n<p>Jitter is a deviation in timing. For sampling, it can be defined as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mi>T<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j_k=r_k-(r_0+kT)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nor as the deviation of the intervals\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><mi>T<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r_{k+1}-r_k-T<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThese two quantities must be distinguished. In the case study, releases\nare ideally periodic; the <em>start latency and response time<\/em> vary.\nThis is not the same as sampling jitter.<\/p>\n<p>A hard real-time system must guarantee that its deadlines are met\nunder the specified conditions. With soft deadlines, occasional late\nresults may reduce quality. A mean alone is not proof: with 99 responses\nin 3 ms and one in 503 ms, the mean is 8 ms but the maximum is 503\nms.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Utilisation and response time<\/h2>\n<p>For periodic tasks on a single CPU, the modelled utilisation is<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><munder><mo>∑<\/mo><mi>i<\/mi><\/munder><mfrac><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><\/mfrac><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=\\sum_i\\frac{C_i}{T_i}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U&gt;1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmeans that, with periodic work continuing indefinitely and no jobs being\ndiscarded, one CPU cannot perform the required computation.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U\\le1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ndoes not guarantee feasibility for arbitrary deadlines, priorities,\nblocking or overheads.<\/p>\n<p>For a simple pre-emptive system with fixed priorities, independent\nperiodic tasks, no release jitter and known upper bounds on execution\ntimes, a response-time bound for task\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>i<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ncan be determined iteratively:<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msubsup><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>B<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><msubsup><mi>R<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msubsup><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>B<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><munder><mo>∑<\/mo><mrow><mi>h<\/mi><mo>∈<\/mo><mi>h<\/mi><mi>p<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>i<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/munder><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">⌈<\/mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>R<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msubsup><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>h<\/mi><\/msub><\/mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">⌉<\/mo><\/mrow><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>h<\/mi><\/msub><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_i^{(0)}=C_i+B_i,\\qquad R_i^{(k+1)}=C_i+B_i+\\sum_{h\\in hp(i)}\\left\\lceil\\frac{R_i^{(k)}}{T_h}\\right\\rceil C_h.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h<\/mi><mi>p<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>i<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">hp(i)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ndenotes the higher-priority tasks, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>B<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_i<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis an assumed upper bound on blocking time. Each higher-priority task\nmay require up to the indicated number of executions within the window\nunder consideration. Iteration stops at the fixed point or when the\ndeadline is exceeded; in the latter case, this procedure provides no\nproof that the deadline is met. For this example, deadlines are assumed\nnot to exceed periods. Overheads must be accounted for separately unless\nalready included in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_i<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>B<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_i<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Example:<\/strong> Three tasks, highest priority first:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_1=5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_1=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_2=8<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_2=2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>20<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_3=20<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_3=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_3=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D_3=10<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.60<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=0.60<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe iteration for the third task is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mo>→<\/mo><mn>7<\/mn><mo>→<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><mo>→<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4\\to7\\to8\\to8<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms. The deadline is met under the model assumptions. With\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_3=4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms, iteration starts at 7 ms, proceeds as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>7<\/mn><mo>→<\/mo><mn>11<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">7\\to11<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms and exceeds the deadline despite identical CPU utilisation. With\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>B<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_1=B_2=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand deadlines equal to periods, the first two tasks also meet their\ndeadlines:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_1=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_2=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-and-information-technology-en/media/img/U_EIT_100_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Timeline from release to completion and fixed-point iteration of a response-time bound.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Release, actual start and completion define waiting\nand response time; fixed-point iteration estimates a deadline under\nadditional workload.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>From estimation to testing<\/h2>\n<p>An analytical bound is only as reliable as its parameters. The\nexecution time of a host program is not the worst-case execution time\n(WCET) of a microcontroller. On the target system, cache behaviour,\nflash wait states, interrupt masking, compiler optimisation, DMA bus\naccesses and contention affect timing. Timestamps with a reliably\ncalibrated time base, traces or GPIO measurements reveal observed\ntimings. Even extensive testing does not prove complete coverage of all\noperating conditions.<\/p>\n<p>A minimum report includes the number of generated, processed and lost\nsamples, deadline misses, definitions of the timing quantities, mean and\nmaximum values, and peak queue occupancy. Quantiles are useful when the\nsample size and operating conditions are documented. Losses must not\ndisappear from performance evaluation: a sensible success metric relates\non-time completed samples to the <strong>generated<\/strong> samples.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Application: non-pre-emptive consumer<\/h2>\n<p>The sensor node in the following lesson uses a single serial consumer\nrather than a pre-emptive multitasking scheduler. Its waiting time\nbefore starting can increase because of queue occupancy or blocking of\njob starts. Once processing of a record has begun, it runs to completion\nwithout interruption in the model. The pre-emptive response-time\nanalysis above must not be applied to this case without adaptation.\nInstead, release, queue and completion events are simulated\ndirectly.<\/p>\n<p>In normal operation, with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_s=10<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms and a free consumer,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_k=3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms for all samples. Blocking job starts for three milliseconds exactly\nat release produces\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_k=6<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms for that sample. Both values are below the model deadline of 8 ms.\nFor prolonged start blocking or chronic overload, these individual\ncalculations are insufficient; see <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M24&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M24-L5<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises and checks<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>20<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=20<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>24<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s=24<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>27<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=27<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D=6<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms. <strong>Solution:<\/strong> Start latency 4 ms, response time 7 ms,\ndeadline missed by 1 ms.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Two periodic tasks with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mi>T<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C/T=2/5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3/4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\n<strong>Solution:<\/strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1.15<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=1.15<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nimpossible on one CPU if jobs must continue to be performed\nindefinitely.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">In the fixed-point example above, let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D_3=8<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms. <strong>Solution:<\/strong> Fixed point 8 ms; deadline met exactly\nunder the assumptions.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A node generates 100 samples, loses 2 and completes another 5 too\nlate. <strong>Solution:<\/strong> 93% on-time complete results. A\nfraction based on the 98 received samples would conceal the effect of\nlosses.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.vvz.ethz.ch/Vorlesungsverzeichnis/lerneinheit.view?ansicht=KATALOGDATEN&amp;lang=en&amp;lerneinheitId=204662&amp;semkez=2026W\">ETH\nZürich – Embedded Systems, 227-0124-00L (Curriculum G5)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://freertos.org/Documentation/02-Kernel/04-API-references/02-Task-control/02-vTaskDelayUntil\">FreeRTOS\n– vTaskDelayUntil<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://arm-software.github.io/CMSIS_6/latest/Core/group__NVIC__gr.html\">Arm\nCMSIS-Core – Interrupts and Exceptions (NVIC)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_en:M24-L5":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L5\">M24-L5 – Practical Assignment: Testing Data and Timestamps of a Simulated Sensor Node<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M24 – Bachelor–Master Bridge: Transition to Embedded Systems<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor · Bachelor–Master Bridge<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M24&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M24-L1<\/a>\nthrough <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering&amp;module=M24&amp;lesson=L4&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M24-L4<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Run a reproducible C model,\ncheck data integrity and timing constraints, and explain design\nlimitations.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Assignment and verifiable specification<\/h2>\n<p>Develop a simulation that runs on a host computer for a measurement\nnode whose hardware timer ideally generates one sample every 10 ms.\nActual device peripherals, sensor physics and conversion duration are\nnot part of the model. The ADC code\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1000<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>37<\/mn><mi>k<\/mi><mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">mod<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mn>500<\/mn><\/mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1000+(37k\\bmod500)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis a deterministic synthetic test sequence used to detect data\ncorruption and swaps. The timestamp is the ideal sampling time\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mi>k<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r_k=10k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms. The source generates 100 samples,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nto 99. The consumer retrieves data from a FIFO queue with four waiting\nslots and can additionally process exactly one active sample.<\/p>\n<p>Requirements: preserve order, prevent silent losses, pass timestamps\non unchanged, and achieve a response time of at most 8 ms in the\nintended normal operating conditions. When the queue is full, the newly\narriving sample is discarded. The consumer does not suspend the source.\nA deadline miss and a loss are two distinct error categories; the\ndeadline is inclusive. The simulation uses integer milliseconds and\nprocesses simultaneous events in this order: arrival, completion, then\npossible start. Blocking affects only the start of a job; an active job\nis not interrupted.<\/p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Case<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Service time<\/th>\n<th>Start blocking<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>0 Normal<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">3 ms<\/td>\n<td>None<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1 Periodic<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">3 ms<\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t<\/mi><mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">mod<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mn>40<\/mn><\/mrow><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t\\bmod40&lt;3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 Service gap<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">3 ms<\/td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>30<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>89<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">30\\le t&lt;89<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 Overload<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">12 ms<\/td>\n<td>None<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>The time limit of 3000 ms allows all accepted samples to be drained;\nreaching it with unfinished work is considered an error.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Reference calculation and invariants<\/h2>\n<p>For the free consumer without a backlog,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mi>C<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_k=r_k+C<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIn the periodic case, 25 of 100 releases are followed by a start delay\nof 3 ms; 75 responses take 3 ms and 25 take 6 ms. This gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mover><mi>R<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾<\/mo><\/mover><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>75<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>25<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mn>100<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3.75<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\bar R=(75\\cdot3+25\\cdot6)/100=3.75<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms. During the service gap, six samples arrive before the next service\nbegins, four of which are stored. The first completion is at 92 ms for\nthe sample from 30 ms, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">max<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>62<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_{\\max}=62<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nms. The stored samples from 40, 50 and 60 ms complete at 95, 98 and 101\nms. The sample at 90 ms completes at 104 ms; the following sample at 100\nms completes at 107 ms and meets the deadline again. The two lost\nsamples are 7 and 8. In the overload case,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>12<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>10<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1.2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=12/10=1.2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\neven with an empty queue, every response takes longer than 8 ms.<\/p>\n<p>The following invariants must be checked: FIFO occupancy between zero\nand four; consecutive sequence numbers at generation; strictly\nincreasing sequence numbers and correct payload data at completion;\nafter draining,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N_{\\mathrm{erzeugt}}=N_{\\mathrm{fertig}}+N_{\\mathrm{verloren}}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe number of missing sequence numbers, including any gaps at the\nbeginning or end, must match the loss count. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N_{\\mathrm{fertig}}&gt;0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mover><mi>R<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾<\/mo><\/mover><mo>=<\/mo><mo>∑<\/mo><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mi>/<\/mi><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\bar R=\\sum R_k/N_{\\mathrm{fertig}}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe success fraction is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mspace width=\"0.222em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ä<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q=(N_{\\mathrm{fertig}}-N_{\\mathrm{zu\\ spät}})/N_{\\mathrm{erzeugt}}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe original subscripts erzeugt, fertig, verloren and zu spät mean\ngenerated, completed, lost and late, respectively.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Reproducible C11 program<\/h2>\n<p>Save the program as <code>sensor.c<\/code>. It requires a C11\nimplementation supporting the fixed-width types used. With GCC or Clang,\nfor example, compile it using\n<code>cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic sensor.c -o sensor<\/code>\nand run it using <code>./sensor<\/code>. With GCC,\n<code>-fsanitize=undefined<\/code> can also be enabled. Assertions must\nremain active (no <code>-DNDEBUG<\/code>). The queue is correctly\nsynchronised only within the simulated sequential execution; it is\n<strong>not ISR-safe production code<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre class=\"sourceCode c\"><code class=\"sourceCode c\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><a href=\"#cb1-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"pp\">#include <\/span><span class=\"im\">&lt;assert.h&gt;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"><a href=\"#cb1-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"pp\">#include <\/span><span class=\"im\">&lt;stdint.h&gt;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-3\"><a href=\"#cb1-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"pp\">#include <\/span><span class=\"im\">&lt;stdbool.h&gt;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-4\"><a href=\"#cb1-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"pp\">#include <\/span><span class=\"im\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"><a href=\"#cb1-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"pp\">#define CAP <\/span><span class=\"dv\">4<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-6\"><a href=\"#cb1-6\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"pp\">#define N <\/span><span class=\"dv\">100<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-7\"><a href=\"#cb1-7\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"pp\">#define PERIOD <\/span><span class=\"dv\">10<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-8\"><a href=\"#cb1-8\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"pp\">#define DEADLINE <\/span><span class=\"dv\">8<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-9\"><a href=\"#cb1-9\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">typedef<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">struct<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">uint32_t<\/span> seq<span class=\"op\">,<\/span> stamp<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">uint16_t<\/span> adc<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">}<\/span> Sample<span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-10\"><a href=\"#cb1-10\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">typedef<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">struct<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span> Sample a<span class=\"op\">[<\/span>CAP<span class=\"op\">];<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">unsigned<\/span> head<span class=\"op\">,<\/span> tail<span class=\"op\">,<\/span> count<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">}<\/span> Queue<span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-11\"><a href=\"#cb1-11\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"dt\">static<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">bool<\/span> push<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>Queue <span class=\"op\">*<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">,<\/span> Sample s<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-12\"><a href=\"#cb1-12\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span><span class=\"op\">(<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">-&gt;<\/span>count <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> CAP<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">false<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-13\"><a href=\"#cb1-13\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    q<span class=\"op\">-&gt;<\/span>a<span class=\"op\">[<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">-&gt;<\/span>head<span class=\"op\">]<\/span> <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> s<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> q<span class=\"op\">-&gt;<\/span>head <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"op\">(<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">-&gt;<\/span>head<span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">)%<\/span>CAP<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">++<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">-&gt;<\/span>count<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">true<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-14\"><a href=\"#cb1-14\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-15\"><a href=\"#cb1-15\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"dt\">static<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">bool<\/span> pop<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>Queue <span class=\"op\">*<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">,<\/span> Sample <span class=\"op\">*<\/span>s<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-16\"><a href=\"#cb1-16\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span><span class=\"op\">(!<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">-&gt;<\/span>count<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">false<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-17\"><a href=\"#cb1-17\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"op\">*<\/span>s<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">-&gt;<\/span>a<span class=\"op\">[<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">-&gt;<\/span>tail<span class=\"op\">];<\/span> q<span class=\"op\">-&gt;<\/span>tail<span class=\"op\">=(<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">-&gt;<\/span>tail<span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">)%<\/span>CAP<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">--<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">-&gt;<\/span>count<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">true<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-18\"><a href=\"#cb1-18\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-19\"><a href=\"#cb1-19\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"dt\">static<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">uint16_t<\/span> code<span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dt\">uint32_t<\/span> seq<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dt\">uint16_t<\/span><span class=\"op\">)(<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1000<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">+(<\/span><span class=\"dv\">37<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>seq<span class=\"op\">)%<\/span><span class=\"dv\">500<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">);<\/span> <span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-20\"><a href=\"#cb1-20\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"dt\">static<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">bool<\/span> blocked<span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dt\">unsigned<\/span> mode<span class=\"op\">,<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">uint32_t<\/span> t<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-21\"><a href=\"#cb1-21\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"op\">(<\/span>mode<span class=\"op\">==<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span> <span class=\"op\">&amp;&amp;<\/span> t<span class=\"op\">%<\/span><span class=\"dv\">40<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span><span class=\"dv\">3<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">||<\/span> <span class=\"op\">(<\/span>mode<span class=\"op\">==<\/span><span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span> <span class=\"op\">&amp;&amp;<\/span> t<span class=\"op\">&gt;=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">30<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span> <span class=\"op\">&amp;&amp;<\/span> t<span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span><span class=\"dv\">89<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">);<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-22\"><a href=\"#cb1-22\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-23\"><a href=\"#cb1-23\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"dt\">static<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">void<\/span> run<span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dt\">unsigned<\/span> mode<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-24\"><a href=\"#cb1-24\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    Queue q<span class=\"op\">={<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">};<\/span> Sample active<span class=\"op\">={<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">};<\/span> <span class=\"dt\">bool<\/span> busy<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"kw\">false<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-25\"><a href=\"#cb1-25\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"dt\">uint32_t<\/span> finish<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span> last<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span> maxlat<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span> sumlat<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-26\"><a href=\"#cb1-26\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"dt\">unsigned<\/span> sent<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span> lost<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span> done<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span> late<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span> peak<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span> gaps<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-27\"><a href=\"#cb1-27\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"dt\">unsigned<\/span> service<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>mode<span class=\"op\">==<\/span><span class=\"dv\">3<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">?<\/span><span class=\"dv\">12<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">:<\/span><span class=\"dv\">3<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-28\"><a href=\"#cb1-28\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span><span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dt\">uint32_t<\/span> t<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span> t<span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span><span class=\"dv\">3000<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">++<\/span>t<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-29\"><a href=\"#cb1-29\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span><span class=\"op\">(<\/span>t<span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span>N<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>PERIOD <span class=\"op\">&amp;&amp;<\/span> t<span class=\"op\">%<\/span>PERIOD<span class=\"op\">==<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-30\"><a href=\"#cb1-30\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            Sample s<span class=\"op\">={<\/span>sent<span class=\"op\">,<\/span>t<span class=\"op\">,<\/span>code<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>sent<span class=\"op\">)};<\/span> <span class=\"op\">++<\/span>sent<span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-31\"><a href=\"#cb1-31\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span><span class=\"op\">(!<\/span>push<span class=\"op\">(&amp;<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">,<\/span>s<span class=\"op\">))<\/span> <span class=\"op\">++<\/span>lost<span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-32\"><a href=\"#cb1-32\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span><span class=\"op\">(<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>count<span class=\"op\">&gt;<\/span>peak<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> peak<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>count<span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-33\"><a href=\"#cb1-33\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-34\"><a href=\"#cb1-34\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span><span class=\"op\">(<\/span>busy <span class=\"op\">&amp;&amp;<\/span> t<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>finish<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-35\"><a href=\"#cb1-35\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"dt\">uint32_t<\/span> lat<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>t<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>active<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>stamp<span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-36\"><a href=\"#cb1-36\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            assert<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>active<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>adc<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>code<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>active<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>seq<span class=\"op\">));<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-37\"><a href=\"#cb1-37\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            assert<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>active<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>stamp<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>active<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>seq<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>PERIOD<span class=\"op\">);<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-38\"><a href=\"#cb1-38\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span><span class=\"op\">(<\/span>done<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span> assert<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>active<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>seq<span class=\"op\">&gt;<\/span>last<span class=\"op\">);<\/span> gaps<span class=\"op\">+=<\/span>active<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>seq<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>last<span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-39\"><a href=\"#cb1-39\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">else<\/span> gaps<span class=\"op\">+=<\/span>active<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>seq<span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-40\"><a href=\"#cb1-40\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            last<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>active<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>seq<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">++<\/span>done<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> sumlat<span class=\"op\">+=<\/span>lat<span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-41\"><a href=\"#cb1-41\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span><span class=\"op\">(<\/span>lat<span class=\"op\">&gt;<\/span>maxlat<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> maxlat<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>lat<span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-42\"><a href=\"#cb1-42\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span><span class=\"op\">(<\/span>lat<span class=\"op\">&gt;<\/span>DEADLINE<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">++<\/span>late<span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-43\"><a href=\"#cb1-43\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            busy<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"kw\">false<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-44\"><a href=\"#cb1-44\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-45\"><a href=\"#cb1-45\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span><span class=\"op\">(!<\/span>busy <span class=\"op\">&amp;&amp;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">!<\/span>blocked<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>mode<span class=\"op\">,<\/span>t<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">&amp;&amp;<\/span> pop<span class=\"op\">(&amp;<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">,&amp;<\/span>active<span class=\"op\">))<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-46\"><a href=\"#cb1-46\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            busy<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"kw\">true<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span> finish<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>t<span class=\"op\">+<\/span>service<span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-47\"><a href=\"#cb1-47\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-48\"><a href=\"#cb1-48\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span><span class=\"op\">(<\/span>sent<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>N <span class=\"op\">&amp;&amp;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">!<\/span>busy <span class=\"op\">&amp;&amp;<\/span> q<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>count<span class=\"op\">==<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">break<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-49\"><a href=\"#cb1-49\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-50\"><a href=\"#cb1-50\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    assert<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>sent<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>N <span class=\"op\">&amp;&amp;<\/span> done<span class=\"op\">+<\/span>lost<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>sent <span class=\"op\">&amp;&amp;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">!<\/span>busy <span class=\"op\">&amp;&amp;<\/span> <span class=\"op\">!<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>count<span class=\"op\">);<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-51\"><a href=\"#cb1-51\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    gaps<span class=\"op\">+=<\/span>N<span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">-<\/span>last<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> assert<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>gaps<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>lost<span class=\"op\">);<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-52\"><a href=\"#cb1-52\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    printf<span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"st\">&quot;<\/span><span class=\"sc\">%u<\/span><span class=\"st\">,<\/span><span class=\"sc\">%u<\/span><span class=\"st\">,<\/span><span class=\"sc\">%u<\/span><span class=\"st\">,<\/span><span class=\"sc\">%u<\/span><span class=\"st\">,<\/span><span class=\"sc\">%u<\/span><span class=\"st\">,<\/span><span class=\"sc\">%u<\/span><span class=\"st\">,<\/span><span class=\"sc\">%u<\/span><span class=\"st\">,<\/span><span class=\"sc\">%u\\n<\/span><span class=\"st\">&quot;<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span>mode<span class=\"op\">,<\/span>sent<span class=\"op\">,<\/span>done<span class=\"op\">,<\/span>lost<span class=\"op\">,<\/span>late<span class=\"op\">,<\/span>peak<span class=\"op\">,<\/span>maxlat<span class=\"op\">,<\/span>sumlat<span class=\"op\">);<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-53\"><a href=\"#cb1-53\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-54\"><a href=\"#cb1-54\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"dt\">int<\/span> main<span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dt\">void<\/span><span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-55\"><a href=\"#cb1-55\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    Queue q<span class=\"op\">={<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">};<\/span> Sample s<span class=\"op\">={<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">};<\/span> assert<span class=\"op\">(!<\/span>pop<span class=\"op\">(&amp;<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">,&amp;<\/span>s<span class=\"op\">));<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-56\"><a href=\"#cb1-56\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span><span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dt\">unsigned<\/span> i<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span>i<span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span>CAP<span class=\"op\">;++<\/span>i<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> assert<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>push<span class=\"op\">(&amp;<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">,(<\/span>Sample<span class=\"op\">){<\/span>i<span class=\"op\">,<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">}));<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-57\"><a href=\"#cb1-57\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    assert<span class=\"op\">(!<\/span>push<span class=\"op\">(&amp;<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">,(<\/span>Sample<span class=\"op\">){<\/span><span class=\"dv\">99<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">}));<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-58\"><a href=\"#cb1-58\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span><span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dt\">unsigned<\/span> i<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span>i<span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span>CAP<span class=\"op\">;++<\/span>i<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> <span class=\"op\">{<\/span> assert<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>pop<span class=\"op\">(&amp;<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">,&amp;<\/span>s<span class=\"op\">));<\/span> assert<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>s<span class=\"op\">.<\/span>seq<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>i<span class=\"op\">);<\/span> <span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-59\"><a href=\"#cb1-59\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    assert<span class=\"op\">(!<\/span>pop<span class=\"op\">(&amp;<\/span>q<span class=\"op\">,&amp;<\/span>s<span class=\"op\">));<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-60\"><a href=\"#cb1-60\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"dt\">uint32_t<\/span> start<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>UINT32_MAX<span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">,<\/span> now<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-61\"><a href=\"#cb1-61\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    assert<span class=\"op\">((<\/span><span class=\"dt\">uint32_t<\/span><span class=\"op\">)(<\/span>now<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>start<span class=\"op\">)==<\/span><span class=\"dv\">5<\/span><span class=\"bu\">u<\/span><span class=\"op\">);<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-62\"><a href=\"#cb1-62\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    puts<span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"st\">&quot;mode,sent,done,lost,late,peak,maxlat,sumlat&quot;<\/span><span class=\"op\">);<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-63\"><a href=\"#cb1-63\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span><span class=\"op\">(<\/span><span class=\"dt\">unsigned<\/span> m<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span>m<span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span><span class=\"dv\">4<\/span><span class=\"op\">;++<\/span>m<span class=\"op\">)<\/span> run<span class=\"op\">(<\/span>m<span class=\"op\">);<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-64\"><a href=\"#cb1-64\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"op\">}<\/span><\/span><\/code><\/pre><\/div>\n<p>The program checks payload data, timestamps, sequence order, the loss\nbalance, empty and full FIFO states, and tick wraparound. Starting at\nindex 0 and performing numerous write and read operations also checks\nindex wraparound in the scenarios. The console output contains one CSV\nrow per model case. <code>sumlat<\/code> sums only response times of\ncompleted records. A real implementation would require a defined API\nwith separate timekeeping, hardware abstraction, ISR handover and\nprocessing.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Results and interpretation<\/h2>\n<p>Executed host reference simulation (100 samples per scenario):<\/p>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-9\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-12\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-12\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-12\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-12\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-12\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-12\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-12\">\n<\/colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Case<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Completed<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Lost<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Late<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Peak queue<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Max R (ms)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Mean R (ms)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">On time<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Normal<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">3<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">3.00<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100%<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Periodic<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">6<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">3.75<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100%<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Service gap<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">98<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">2<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">5<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">4<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">62<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">5.13<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">93%<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Overload<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">87<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">13<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">87<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">4<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">58<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">48.69<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0%<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>Peak occupancy is measured after arrival and before removal. The mean\nresponse time of approximately 5.13 ms after the service gap is below\nthe deadline, yet five results miss the deadline and two are missing. In\nthe overload case, neither the completed nor the lost samples meet the\nrequirements. Increasing the buffer size may reduce losses during a\nlimited service gap, but the delay of additionally stored older samples\ncan increase. With sustained\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U&gt;1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\na finite-capacity queue will still overflow. A shorter maximum blocking\ninterval, faster processing, dividing the work or changing the sampling\nfrequency should be considered; reducing the frequency, however, changes\nthe signal-theory requirements.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-and-information-technology-en/media/img/U_EIT_101_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Comparison of four operating cases by on-time, late and lost samples and maximum response time.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Four synthetic sensor-node cases distinguish\non-time, late and lost samples; a good average response time does not\nestablish deadline compliance.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Independent extensions and submission<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Change the queue capacity to 6 and retest case 2. Expected: all six\narrivals during the service gap fit. At the 90 ms arrival, one sample is\nalready being processed; the buffer can accommodate this arrival too. No\nlosses, but some deadlines are still missed. Compare the deadline\nstatistics with the reference.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Change the service time in the overload case to 7 ms. Expected with\nunblocked starts: all 100 samples complete in 7 ms, with no losses or\ndeadline misses.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Add the number of on-time results and the maximum interval between\nsampling timestamps of retained samples to the CSV output. Expected in\ncase 2: 93 on time; largest gap 30 ms between samples 6 and 9.\nDistinguish this gap test from completion timing.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Test an intentionally incorrect timestamp or sequence number and\nexplain which assertion detects it. A positive test alone does not\nestablish that faults are detected.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>Submission: specification with event order, C file, compilation\ncommand and output for the four reference cases, two selected variants\nand a reasoned evaluation. Record the compiler, changes and aspects not\ntested. Assessment criteria: 25% correct data integrity, 25% timing\ndefinitions and event order, 25% reproducible tests with evaluation, 25%\nreasoned limitations and follow-up measures. No actual ADC, interrupt or\nWCET measurements were performed; these remain a separate validation\nstep for the later master’s specialisation M29.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.vvz.ethz.ch/Vorlesungsverzeichnis/lerneinheit.view?ansicht=KATALOGDATEN&amp;lang=en&amp;lerneinheitId=204662&amp;semkez=2026W\">ETH\nZürich – Embedded Systems, 227-0124-00L (Curriculum G5)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://avrdudes.github.io/avr-libc/avr-libc-user-manual/group__util__atomic.html\">AVR-LibC\n– Atomic Blocks<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://freertos.org/Documentation/02-Kernel/04-API-references/02-Task-control/02-vTaskDelayUntil\">FreeRTOS\n– vTaskDelayUntil<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://community.freertos.org/Documentation/02-Kernel/04-API-references/06-Queues/06-xQueueSendToBackFromISR\">FreeRTOS\n– xQueueSendToBackFromISR<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a><\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>"};
